  senderType: 0
  phishingType: 0
  subjects:
  - 'From: AIPhishingBot@XCEL.Com

    To: Admin@XCEL.Com

    **AUTOMATED MESSAGE**'
  greetings:
  - "Attention Admin! The network is disabled. A message from your supervisor reads
    as follows: So, you won\u2019t believe this, but our head of security fell for
    a phishing scam. Can\u2019t believe this\u2026 \n\nGoing to have to start calling
    him old at this point; but looking at the investigation so far, it looks like
    they used an AI system to clone my voice and get into his systems to get info
    on him and just steal it which is crazy! \n\nI have heard about phishing scams
    just stealing info but never just acting like someone else in this way to get
    your own info, while behaving like you and then just getting access to everything!\n\nThe
    company is shuttering the servers now because of it, so they\u2019re gonna fix
    the data breach. Gotta send this message through the AI, but looks like we gotta
    kill time. But still,\nCrazy world\u2026"
  part1s:
  - "AI voice cloning? Didn\u2019t even think that could be used like that\u2026"
  part2s:
  - Dang, this guy really is showing his age, but honestly that AI stuff is pretty
    new.
  part3s:
  - "Make sure they didn\u2019t get into your stuff as well. We should have a way
    to confirm if who we\u2019re talking to is real."
  signoffs:
  - Hi
  phishing:
  - No
